# Commit messages

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) and keep the **subject line at most 50 characters** (enforced by `commitlint.config.cjs`).

## Format

```
type(scope): subject

Optional body wrapped at ~72 columns. Explain why, not what.
```

- **type**: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, …
- **scope**: optional area (`form`, `button`, `select`, …)
- **subject**: imperative, lowercase, no trailing period

## Examples

```
feat(form): honor fieldset disable via callback
fix(button): sync shadow control on form disable
docs: add ADR for composite member submission
```

## Avoid

```
Deepen form control lifecycle seam and fix fieldset disable propagation.
```

Too long (72 chars), not conventional, no type prefix.

## Before committing

```bash
echo "feat(form): short subject here" | yarn commitlint
```